# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the HYBRID_SANITIZE CI leg (issue #42).
#
# The sanitizer build instruments the hybrid provider and its tests, but NOT
# OpenSSL, liboqs, or the PQ-only oqsprovider. Any leak whose allocation is rooted
# in one of those libraries (one-time provider/init state we neither own nor free)
# is out of scope for the provider memory-safety audit, so it is suppressed here
# by originating module. Leaks rooted in the provider's own code are NOT matched by
# these rules and will still fail the run — which is the point of the leg.
leak:libcrypto
leak:libssl
leak:liboqs
leak:oqsprovider
